Package: os7-setup
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: @OS7_ARCH@
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: @OS7_ICU@
Recommends: os7-console (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: The OS/7 text-mode installer
 os7-setup, the program the setup medium starts on tty1: an OS/7-authored text
 phase styled after MS-DOS 6.22 Setup and the Windows 2000 text phase, which
 partitions the disk, creates the ZFS-on-LUKS layout, unpacks the system,
 installs the bootloader and writes the boot-environment menu.
 .
 A NativeAOT binary of about 3.4 MB with no .NET runtime beneath it, which is
 what makes it viable as the first thing that runs on a machine — the medium
 carries no runtime at all. It links against ICU because it is built with
 InvariantGlobalization=false, and without it the program does not start.
 .
 os7-console is a Recommends rather than a Depends because Setup carries its own
 palette and font handling and applies them itself: on a virtual console it
 calls setvtrgb and setfont, and on anything else it emits the same palette
 indices as SGR. It looks right on a medium that has the fonts and works on one
 that does not.
